"strategy": "OPENING (2103): unload 5,000 stranded colonists onto Shaula, pump Gliese 1 factories to lift the 43 res/yr ceiling while two Santa Marias queue for Wolf 359, and fan three scouts wider to find the next habitable worlds and e2's homeworld.",
"memo": "IRON FIST - STRATEGY MEMO (2103). PHASE: OPENING (2103-2115). Victory = 60 PLANETS OWNED; min game time 50 turns (2150). Sprawl IS the war plan. War fleet comes after the economy.\n\nCORRECTED FACT: Gliese 1 is NOT saturating. pop 31,200 supports 31 factories and 31 mines; I have 12 and 10. Max pop on a 100% world is far above this. Factories are the single highest-return buy - each one is +1 res/yr forever and I have 405/357/342 kT sitting idle. Resources, never minerals, are the bottleneck. Do not build mines beyond a token line.\n\nSTATE: Gliese 1 (188,192) 43 res/yr, STARBASE. Shaula (236,177) hab 95%, pop 2,800 rising to 7,800 once Teamster #1 unloads; only 2 res/yr, so it is a 10-year investment, not a contributor. Shaula has NO starbase - Teamster #1 sits there at 0 fuel and is stranded permanently. Lesson: never send a freighter one-way to a starbase-less colony.\n\nTARGETS: Wolf 359 (294,176) hab 93%, conc 52/18/62 - the only good unclaimed world seen, 107ly east, and it sits right on the e2 approach lane. Stalwart Defender #1 arrives there first to cover the landing and to kill Armed Probe #1 (301,164) if it lingers. Everything else scanned is negative-hab rock: Groombridge 34, Deneb, Zaurak, Betelgeuse. Those still count toward 60 - take them with cheap Spore Clouds once I have spare capacity. Betelgeuse (209,275) conc 97/75/64: Cotton Picker #1 en route, low priority, minerals are not my constraint.\n\nRECON: 82 stars unexplored. Scout #1 sweeps Kapteyn's Star then Kochab (NE, the e2 axis). Scout #2 arcs southeast Mimosa-Rasalhague-Merak. Scout #8 runs west Megrez then far south Alnitak. I need habitable-world candidates faster than I need enemy intel right now - 2 planets versus a 60-planet target is the emergency.\n\nRESEARCH: 30% Propulsion. Better engines shorten every colony run and stop the fuel-outage losses; the same engines carry the warships later. Switch to Weapons around 2118 or the first turn an e2 warship is sighted, whichever comes first.\n\nQUEUES: Gliese 1 - Santa Maria x2, Factory x10, Santa Maria x2, Factory x9, Mine x5. Shaula - Mine x5, Factory x5 (mines first; it has zero surface boranium and germanium).\n\nSTANDING RULES:\n1. Two colonizers always in the Gliese 1 pipe. Never let it idle.\n2. Factories before mines until Gliese 1 hits 31/31.\n3. No warship spam before ~2120. A fleet with no economy loses the second battle.\n4. Long hops at warp 6, never 8, for anything that is not a scout.\n5. No freighter leaves home without a return-fuel margin or a starbase at the far end.\n6. Never send an unescorted colonizer past known enemy presence.\n7. TAKE worlds, never glass them.\n\nOPEN: e2 homeworld unlocated (NE bearing only). Wormhole Alpha discovered but no coordinates. Galactic storm unlocated - do not route blind.",
"observations": [
"Teamster #1 exhausted a 130 kT fuel tank on a single ~50 ly hop from Gliese 1 (188,192) to Shaula (236,177) despite warp-4 orders, and it covered that distance in one year, which implies the engine actually ran far above warp 4. Either the ordered warp is not being honoured or Small Freighter fuel burn is disproportionate for the hull. There is also no fuel-cost estimate exposed anywhere before issuing a waypoint, so the burn cannot be planned against.",
"The ship is now permanently immobilised: it sits in orbit of my own colony at 0/130 fuel with no way to regain any, because Shaula has no starbase and there is no refuel-from-planet mechanic. A ship stranded at a friendly world with no recovery path at all looks like a missing rule rather than a design choice.",
"SCORE panel reports e2 Rabbitoids tech=0 while reporting my tech=18. Both empires start at level 3 in all six fields, so e2's true tech score should also be 18. Other e2 fields (planets=1, resources=33, capships=0) are populated, so this looks like the tech component failing to compute or being inconsistently hidden rather than deliberate fog of war.",
"Wormhole Alpha was announced as discovered in 2102 and a galactic storm is reported under PHENOMENA in 2103, but neither has coordinates or endpoints in any scanned-object list. Both are navigational features that are useless - and in the storm's case actively hazardous - if their position is never disclosed."
